MonkSynth for Schwung
=====================

The DSP in src/dsp/{synth,voice,delay}.{c,h} and src/dsp/synth_internal.h is
vendored VERBATIM and is not modified here.

  Upstream:    MonkSynth by Jonathan Taylor
               https://github.com/JonET/monksynth
  Via:         MonkSynth for iOS by Charles Vestal
               https://github.com/charlesvestal/monksynth-ios
  Licence:     MIT (see LICENSE)

MonkSynth is itself an homage to the Delay Lama VST plug-in by AudioNerdz
(2002).

The twelve characters' voices are ported verbatim from the iOS port's
CharacterVoiceTable (six hand-tuned) and FactoryVoiceTable (six of upstream's
own factory patches: Dorje, Jamyang, Monastary, Ngawang, Rabten, Tinley).

The twelve FACES in src/ui/canvas.js are NOT ported art. The iOS characters are
colour bezier drawings with clip masks and alpha, none of which survives a
128x64 1-bit panel, so the silhouettes were re-authored for this display. What
is ported verbatim is the rig behind them -- mouth anchors, mouth centre, mouth
box fraction, eye and head geometry -- because that art is already authored in a
unit square.

